---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PixelField from '@/components/site/PixelField.astro';
import { CodeBlock, Callout } from '@/molecules/DocComponents/DocComponents';
import CtaBanner from '@/components/site/CtaBanner.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Integration Guides - OpenFlows" description="Connect OpenFlows to your existing development tools and workflows.">
  <main>
  <section class="of-page-hero of-dark">
    <PixelField cell={30} density={0.06} />
    <div class="of-container">
      <a href="/developers" class="of-back fade-up">← Developers</a>
      <span class="of-eyebrow fade-up" style="display:flex">Integrations</span>
      <h1 class="fade-up" style="animation-delay:80ms">Connect OpenFlows to your stack.</h1>
      <p class="of-lede fade-up" style="animation-delay:160ms">Setup modes, GitHub, models, notifications and the CLI, with the exact commands and settings.</p>
      <nav class="jump fade-up" style="animation-delay:220ms" aria-label="On this page">
        <a href="#setup" class="of-chip">Setup modes</a>
        <a href="#github" class="of-chip">GitHub</a>
        <a href="#models" class="of-chip">Models</a>
        <a href="#notifications" class="of-chip">Notifications</a>
        <a href="#cli" class="of-chip">CLI</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section style="padding-bottom: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem)">
  <div class="of-container of-container-narrow guide">
    <h2 id="setup">Setup modes</h2>
    <p>One script sets up everything: <code>.env</code> and secrets, GitHub access, Redis and Coder in Docker, your model, the workspace templates and your repository. It is safe to re-run; it skips what is already done.</p>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash">{`# compile from this checkout (default the first time; needs Rust)
./scripts/setup.sh owner/repo --source

# use the published images, no compiling
./scripts/setup.sh owner/repo --compose

# use the release binaries, no compiling
./scripts/setup.sh owner/repo --binary

# pick a version for --compose / --binary (empty = latest release)
OPENFLOWS_VERSION=<version>`}</CodeBlock>

    <h2 id="github">GitHub</h2>
    <p>By default, setup uses the team-owned OpenFlows GitHub App: install it on a repository from the local Console, approve the device code, then choose the repository. No personal App or App secret is needed. To use your own App instead:</p>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash">{`cp .env.example .env
sed -i 's/^OPENFLOWS_GITHUB_AUTH_MODE=.*/OPENFLOWS_GITHUB_AUTH_MODE=self-managed/' .env
./scripts/setup.sh owner/repo`}</CodeBlock>

    <h2 id="models">Models</h2>
    <p>Setup asks for your LLM provider, model and API key once. Keys stay in the Coder AI Gateway; agent workspaces never hold them. You can route FORGE and SENTINEL to different providers so the reviewer does not share the builder’s blind spots.</p>

    <h2 id="notifications">Notifications</h2>
    <p>When a ticket needs a human, OpenFlows can notify Slack, Discord or WhatsApp (through Twilio). Set any of these in <code>.env</code>:</p>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash">{`SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/...
DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=https://discord.com/api/webhooks/...

WHATSAPP_ACCOUNT_SID=...
WHATSAPP_AUTH_TOKEN=...
WHATSAPP_FROM_PHONE=+1...
WHATSAPP_TO_PHONE=+1...`}</CodeBlock>

    <h2 id="cli">CLI</h2>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash">{`openflows              # run the controller (NEXUS and the agent pipeline)
openflows-doctor       # diagnose your environment
./scripts/setup.sh     # set up, upgrade or resume an installation`}</CodeBlock>

    <Callout type="info" title="More Integrations Coming">
      We're working on integrations for Jira, Linear, GitLab, and Bitbucket. <a href="https://github.com/The-AgenticFlow/OpenFlows/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Request an integration ↗</a> on GitHub.
    </Callout>
  </div>
  </section>
  <CtaBanner title="Need an integration we don't have?" body="Jira, Linear, GitLab and Bitbucket are on the roadmap. Tell us what your team needs." primary={{ label: 'Request an integration', href: 'https://github.com/The-AgenticFlow/OpenFlows/issues' }} secondary={{ label: 'Read the docs', href: '/docs' }} />
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .of-back { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .jump { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
  .jump a:hover { color: var(--of-text); border-color: var(--of-mint-line); }
  .guide h2 { margin: 3rem 0 0.75rem; padding-top: 1rem; font-size: 1.5rem; scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--nav-height) + 24px); }
  .guide h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .guide > p { color: var(--of-text-2); margin-bottom: 1rem; }
</style>
